  "limitations": [
    "Remediation of the attempt-01, attempt-02 and attempt-03 findings is documented in docs/planning/reviews/C01/remediation-attempt-01.md, remediation-attempt-02.md and remediation-attempt-03.md. The attempt-03 notes also cover an intermittent test failure found while regenerating evidence (theme applied in a passive effect; now a layout effect with a deterministic regression test) and Codex's three optional suggestions. Superseded native runs are retained with causes under docs/planning/evidence/C01/native-failed/.",
    "The bootstrap agreement run (tools/reference-validator, now with typed record validation, 16 typed resealed cases and two acceptance controls) runs against the actual receipt of this attempt after the verdict, as required before completion; a dry run against a scratch copy of attempt-03 showed both validators rejecting every typed case for the matching type error (attempt-03's own stale fingerprints and failing scores were also reported there, as expected).",
    "Native visual evidence is fixture-only WKWebView self-capture (Fixture > Capture Window), not a screen recording. The snapshot spans the WKWebView's 820pt bounds while web content occupies the 788pt below the title bar (AX: AXWebArea at [95,69] size [1280,788]; the rail fills it to the window bottom), so every capture shows a ~32pt strip at the bottom outside the visible viewport. A rail item may show a pointer-hover fill in captures; aria-current in the AX snapshots identifies the selected destination.",
    "Spoken VoiceOver output was not recorded; accessibility is evidenced through the AX tree (roles, names, aria-current, focus) driven by System Events. Startup network evidence is 0.5s socket sampling over 15s (DNS via mDNSResponder not attributable).",
    "The clean-checkout reproduction uses the same host, account and package/tool caches; it clones the Academy branch fresh from origin and builds a fresh v2 tree configured with the same origin remote.",
    "No signing, notarization, live API, installed-package or SDK work is in C01 scope; those are C02+ and C25-C26."
  ],
